---
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A custom WS2812B word clock built with an Arduino Nano, DS3231 RTC, and capacitive touch controls."
    />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://rsms.me/" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://rsms.me/inter/inter.css" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>WordClock</title>
  </head>

  <body
    class="bg-[#0b1126] text-slate-200 selection:bg-[#aaccff] selection:text-[#113399]"
  >
    <div
      class="mx-auto min-h-screen max-w-screen-xl px-6 py-12 md:px-12 md:py-16 lg:py-0"
    >
      <div class="lg:flex lg:justify-between lg:gap-16">
        <header
          class="lg:sticky lg:top-0 lg:flex lg:h-screen lg:w-[38%] lg:min-w-[360px] lg:flex-col lg:justify-center lg:py-16 mb-10"
        >
          <div
            class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-8 shadow-2xl shadow-blue-950/20 backdrop-blur"
          >
            <div
              class="absolute -right-20 -top-20 h-56 w-56 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 blur-3xl"
            >
            </div>

            <p
              class="mb-6 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Project Writeup
            </p>

            <h1
              class="mb-4 text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl"
            >
              Word<br />Clock
            </h1>

            <p class="max-w-sm text-base leading-7 text-slate-400">
              A quiet, quarter-hour word clock built as a personalized office
              decoration.
            </p>

            <nav class="mt-8 hidden lg:block">
              <div class="space-y-5">
                <a
                  href="#overview"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Overview
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#construction"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Build
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#controls"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Controls
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#code"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Code
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#lessons"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Final Thoughts
                </a>

                <a
                  href="/projects"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#aaccff] transition hover:text-white"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-[#aaccff] transition-all group-hover:w-16"
                  ></span>
                  Return to Projects
                </a>
              </div>
            </nav>
          </div>
        </header>

        <main class="w-full lg:w-[62%] lg:py-24">
          <section id="overview" class="scroll-mt-16">
            <div
              class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035]"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/wordclock-hero.png"
                alt="Word clock sitting on a desk"
                class="aspect-[16/9] w-full object-cover"
              />
            </div>
            <div class="mt-8">
              <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
                I built this word clock for my mom while she was redecorating
                her office around Christmas. I wanted to give her something
                interesting for the space, and after discovering clocks that
                tell time with words, I decided to build my own.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                The project is divided into two parts: construction and code.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="construction" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <div
              class="mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.1fr] md:items-center"
            >
              <div>
                <h2
                  class="mb-8 text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
                >
                  Construction
                </h2>
                <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  The core is an Arduino Nano connected to a DS3231 real-time
                  clock and four TTP223 capacitive touch sensors. It drives an
                  8×8 matrix of WS2812B LEDs from a 5 V adapter.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  I used the layout from mlesniew's word-clock repository as a
                  starting point. Its hidden unlit letters and quarter-hour time
                  resolution made it especially appealing for an office where I
                  wanted the display to stay relatively unobtrusive.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="space-y-4">
                <img
                  src="/images/wordclock-back.png"
                  alt="Back of the word clock showing electronics"
                  class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10"
                />
                <img
                  src="/images/wordclock-layout.png"
                  alt="Word clock letter layout"
                  class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10"
                />
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="controls" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Controls
            </h2>
            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">01</div>
                <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-medium text-white">Brightness</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  The top and bottom-right touch pads control LED brightness.
                </p>
              </article>
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">02</div>
                <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-medium text-white">Color</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  The bottom-left pad cycles through aquamarine, orange,
                  magenta, red, green, and blue.
                </p>
              </article>
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">03</div>
                <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-medium text-white">
                  Time setting
                </h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  The top-left pad switches between time-setting mode and normal
                  operation.
                </p>
              </article>
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">04</div>
                <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-medium text-white">
                  Hour & minute
                </h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  In setting mode, the right-side pads select the hour and
                  minute values.
                </p>
              </article>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
              <img
                src="/images/wordclock-hand.png"
                alt="Word clock being held during construction"
                class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10"
              />
              <img
                src="/images/wordclock-lit.png"
                alt="Word clock displaying the time"
                class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10"
              />
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="code" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Code
            </h2>
            <div
              class="mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1fr_0.8fr] md:items-start"
            >
              <div>
                <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  The clock gets its time from the DS3231 RTC using Adafruit's
                  RTClib and uses FastLED to control the WS2812B matrix.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  I first mapped the physical WS2812B layout and created
                  reference arrays for each word. The controls then map directly
                  to brightness, color, and the time-setting state.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  Because the matrix can only display numbers through twelve,
                  minutes are represented as two digits using the number of
                  illuminated letters in the words “quarter” and the
                  corresponding digit.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500"
                  >Source code</span
                >
                <div class="mt-8 text-xl font-medium text-white break-words">
                  github.com/Padimo/wordclock-ws2812b
                </div>
                <a
                  href="https://github.com/Padimo/wordclock-ws2812b"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noreferrer"
                  class="mt-3 block text-sm text-slate-500 transition hover:text-[#aaccff]"
                >
                  View the project →
                </a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="lessons" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16 pb-24">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Final Thoughts
            </h2>
            <div class="mt-8">
              <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
                This has been one of my most successful projects because it is
                relatively simple while still being a unique addition to the
                original project that inspired it.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                I intentionally left out the original time-change animation and
                front glass panel because I wanted users to see the complete
                layout and because the clock was intended to remain unobtrusive
                during meetings.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                I later used many of the same mechanisms and code for the word
                clock that I integrated into my sunrise alarm clock. At some
                point, I would like to make a larger, higher-quality version
                with minute-level precision.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div
              class="mt-10 flex items-center justify-between border-t border-white/10 pt-6 text-xs text-slate-600"
            >
              <span>WordClock</span>
              <a href="#overview" class="transition hover:text-slate-300"
                >Back to top ↑</a
              >
            </div>
          </section>
        </main>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
